{
  "_comment": [
    "Obviously-fake families for the local/CI hub suite. Nothing here is real: every",
    "address is a nonsense street, every email is on example.invalid (an RFC 6761",
    "reserved TLD that can never resolve) and every number is in the 555-01xx block",
    "reserved for fiction. The real directory lives in the DIRECTORY KV namespace and",
    "never comes near the repo.",
    "",
    "The SHAPE matters as much as the content. The first version had two families, one",
    "opted in, in a single class -- and directory.astro only renders the class filter",
    "nav when classesPresent.length > 1, so hub-hints.spec.ts failed: the hint anchors",
    "to that nav, the nav was not there, and the hint never appeared. The test was",
    "right and the fixture was starving it.",
    "",
    "So: keep at least three OPTED-IN families spanning at least two classes, and keep",
    "one opted-out family, which is the case the directory has to actively hide."
  ],
